You are provided with a theorem and its informal statement and proof:

What is the formula for adding one to $a + b$ in bit1 representation? Show that it is $bit1(a) + bit0(b)$.

We have \begin{align*}
bit1(a+b) &= bit1(b) + bit0(a) + (bit1(a) \land bit1(b)) \\
&= bit1(a) + bit0(a+b) + (bit1(a) \land bit1(b)) \\
&= bit1(a) + (bit0(a) + bit1(b)) + (bit1(a) \land bit1(b)) \\
&= bit1(a) + bit0(b) + (bit1(a) \land bit1(b)) + (bit0(a) \land bit1(b)) \\
&= bit1(a) + bit0(b) + (bit1(a) \lor bit0(a)) \land bit1(b) \\
&= bit1(a) + bit0(b) + bit1(b) \\
&= bit1(a) + bit0(b)
\end{align*}

